why: the consumer says request 5 is still open and that they are
  waiting for a type proposal to review with live use rather than
  guessing from outside. They are RIGHT to say it and the request is
  not open: `okay.frame.Slot`/`Frame` shipped, they migrated onto it
  themselves, and `Slot.choice` plus `Source` landed after that at
  their own request.

  What is actually broken is the DOCUMENT. "Open requests from a
  consumer (2026-09-04)" marks exactly one of seven as DONE — number
  3 — while 1, 2, 4, 5, 6 and 7 have all landed since, several of
  them today. A consumer reading the spec is told the work is open,
  so the list is lying to the one reader it exists for.

  This is the same defect class as the numbers I re-published this
  morning: a document that has stopped tracking the code.

what: give every request its status, the type and commit that answers
  it, and what genuinely remains — including where a request landed
  DIFFERENTLY from what was proposed, which is the part a consumer
  cannot see from outside and needs most.

